In article <AHUTTUNE.90Jul15151624@wonderwoman.hut.fi> ahuttune@niksula.hut.fi (Ari Juhani Huttunen) writes:
>As I see it, the problem is not the rewrite or CPU power. The REAL PROBLEM
>is time used in the dungeon.
>
>A) Players take turns to play.
>   - Playing becomes too slow because you have to wait for all others to act.
>
>B) Playing is done in real time.
>   - This changes nethack into an action game. You could no longer play
>     strategically. Just hit everything in sight.

How about this:
If only one player-character happens to be onscreen, the game would
be as it is now (not real-time).
 
If two or more player characters happen to be onscreen (visible, as
in the same room, etc.), the play mode would switch to a real time
mode. (Maybe, a special command would have to be given to switch
weapons, put-on rings, etc., while the other player(s), as well as 
any monsters which may be around, flail away at you...:-))
